<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>HCCDA-AI Readiness Assessment</title>
<style>
@page { size: A4; margin: 0.7in; }
body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: #102a43; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.35; }
h1 { color: #087f8c; font-size: 25pt; margin-bottom: 4pt; }
h2 { color: #102a43; border-bottom: 2px solid #e76f51; padding-bottom: 4pt; margin-top: 22pt; }
h3 { margin-bottom: 2pt; }
.subtitle { color: #52606d; font-size: 12pt; }
.meta { border: 1px solid #bcccdc; padding: 10pt; margin: 16pt 0; }
.instructions { background: #e8f5f4; padding: 10pt; }
.question { margin: 13pt 0; page-break-inside: avoid; }
.question strong { color: #087f8c; }
.options { margin: 5pt 0 0 18pt; }
.answer-space { color: #52606d; letter-spacing: 2pt; }
table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin-top: 10pt; }
th, td { border: 1px solid #bcccdc; padding: 6pt; text-align: left; }
th { background: #e8f5f4; }
.small { color: #52606d; font-size: 9pt; }
.key { page-break-before: always; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>HCCDA-AI Readiness Assessment</h1>
<div class="subtitle">BSCS entry screening test for HCCDA-AI admission</div>

<div class="meta">
<b>Candidate name:</b> _______________________________________________<br><br>
<b>Student ID / application number:</b> _______________________________<br><br>
<b>Date:</b> ____________________ &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <b>Time started:</b> __________ &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <b>Time finished:</b> __________
</div>

<div class="instructions">
<b>Instructions</b><br>
1. Answer all 20 multiple-choice questions. Select one best answer for each question.<br>
2. Recommended time: 45 minutes. Do not use outside help during the assessment.<br>
3. Each question carries 1 mark. Maximum score: 40 marks.<br>
4. Suggested readiness benchmark: at least 14/20 overall (70%) and at least 3/5 in Logic &amp; Programming (50%).<br>
5. This assessment is a readiness indicator and should be considered with the complete admission process.
</div>

<h2>Section A: Questions</h2>

<div class="question"><b>1. [Logic &amp; programming]</b> A function repeatedly halves n until n becomes 1. Ignoring constants, what is its time complexity?
<div class="options">A. O(1)<br>B. O(log n)<br>C. O(n)<br>D. O(n log n)</div><div class="answer-space">Answer: ______</div></div>

<div class="question"><b>2. [Logic &amp; programming]</b> What is printed by this pseudocode? x = 0; for i = 1 to 4: x = x + i; print(x)
<div class="options">A. 4<br>B. 6<br>C. 10<br>D. 16</div><div class="answer-space">Answer: ______</div></div>

<div class="question"><b>3. [Logic &amp; programming]</b> A queue receives A, B, C in that order. Two items are removed, then D is added. What is removed next?
<div class="options">A. A<br>B. B<br>C. C<br>D. D</div><div class="answer-space">Answer: ______</div></div>

<div class="question"><b>4. [Logic &amp; programming]</b> Which condition is necessary for binary search to work correctly on an array?
<div class="options">A. The array contains only integers<br>B. The array is sorted<br>C. The array has no duplicates<br>D. The array length is even</div><div class="answer-space">Answer: ______</div></div>

<div class="question"><b>5. [Logic &amp; programming]</b> An algorithm returns the first repeated value in [4, 2, 7, 2, 9, 4]. Which value should it return if it scans from left to right?
<div class="options">A. 2<br>B. 4<br>C. 7<br>D. 9</div><div class="answer-space">Answer: ______</div></div>

<div class="question"><b>6. [Data structures &amp; algorithms]</b> Which data structure is most suitable for checking whether brackets are properly nested?
<div class="options">A. Stack<br>B. Queue<br>C. Graph<br>D. Hash table only</div><div class="answer-space">Answer: ______</div></div>

<div class="question"><b>7. [Data structures &amp; algorithms]</b> A binary search tree has values 8, 3, 10, 1, 6. Which traversal lists the values in ascending order?
<div class="options">A. Preorder<br>B. Postorder<br>C. Inorder<br>D. Level order</div><div class="answer-space">Answer: ______</div></div>

<div class="question"><b>8. [Data structures &amp; algorithms]</b> If an array is already sorted, which common sorting algorithm can finish in O(n) time in its best case?
<div class="options">A. Insertion sort<br>B. Selection sort<br>C. Heap sort<br>D. Merge sort</div><div class="answer-space">Answer: ______</div></div>

<div class="question"><b>9. [Databases]</b> A table stores StudentID, StudentName, and DepartmentName. DepartmentName depends only on DepartmentID, not StudentID. What issue is present?
<div class="options">A. Recursion<br>B. Partial or transitive dependency<br>C. Deadlock<br>D. Packet loss</div><div class="answer-space">Answer: ______</div></div>

<div class="question"><b>10. [Databases]</b> Which SQL clause filters groups after aggregate functions such as COUNT are calculated?
<div class="options">A. WHERE<br>B. ORDER BY<br>C. HAVING<br>D. JOIN</div><div class="answer-space">Answer: ______</div></div>

<div class="question"><b>11. [Operating systems]</b> Three processes each hold one resource and wait for another held by the next process. What is this situation called?
<div class="options">A. Paging<br>B. Deadlock<br>C. Context switching<br>D. Thrashing</div><div class="answer-space">Answer: ______</div></div>

<div class="question"><b>12. [Operating systems]</b> What is the main purpose of virtual memory?
<div class="options">A. To make the CPU clock faster<br>B. To allow programs to use an address space larger than physical RAM<br>C. To permanently store backups<br>D. To encrypt every process</div><div class="answer-space">Answer: ______</div></div>

<div class="question"><b>13. [Computer networks]</b> A browser requests a webpage using HTTPS. Which property does TLS primarily add compared with plain HTTP?
<div class="options">A. Compression only<br>B. Confidentiality and server authentication<br>C. A larger IP address<br>D. Faster DNS lookup</div><div class="answer-space">Answer: ______</div></div>

<div class="question"><b>14. [Computer networks]</b> Which device forwards packets between different IP networks?
<div class="options">A. Hub<br>B. Router<br>C. Keyboard<br>D. Repeater</div><div class="answer-space">Answer: ______</div></div>

<div class="question"><b>15. [Software engineering]</b> A team writes an automated test before implementing the function it tests. Which practice is this?
<div class="options">A. Test-driven development<br>B. Code obfuscation<br>C. Big-bang integration<br>D. Pair deployment</div><div class="answer-space">Answer: ______</div></div>

<div class="question"><b>16. [Software engineering]</b> Which requirement is most measurable and testable?
<div class="options">A. The app should feel modern<br>B. The system should be easy to use<br>C. The report must load within 2 seconds for 95% of requests<br>D. The design should be beautiful</div><div class="answer-space">Answer: ______</div></div>

<div class="question"><b>17. [Discrete math &amp; statistics]</b> A fair coin is tossed twice. What is the probability of getting exactly one head?
<div class="options">A. 1/4<br>B. 1/2<br>C. 2/3<br>D. 3/4</div><div class="answer-space">Answer: ______</div></div>

<div class="question"><b>18. [Discrete math &amp; statistics]</b> If P(A) = 0.6, P(B) = 0.5, and A and B are independent, what is P(A and B)?
<div class="options">A. 0.1<br>B. 0.3<br>C. 0.55<br>D. 1.1</div><div class="answer-space">Answer: ______</div></div>

<div class="question"><b>19. [AI fundamentals]</b> A model performs very well on training data but poorly on unseen data. What is the most likely cause?
<div class="options">A. Underfitting<br>B. Overfitting<br>C. Normalization<br>D. Low variance</div><div class="answer-space">Answer: ______</div></div>

<div class="question"><b>20. [AI fundamentals]</b> In supervised learning, what does a label represent?
<div class="options">A. The target output associated with an example<br>B. The number of CPU cores<br>C. A random feature removed from the data<br>D. The model's learning rate</div><div class="answer-space">Answer: ______</div></div>

<div class="question"><b>21. [Logic &amp; programming]</b> What is the value of 3 AND 5 using bitwise AND?
<div class="options">A. 0<br>B. 1<br>C. 3<br>D. 8</div><div class="answer-space">Answer: ______</div></div>

<div class="question"><b>22. [Logic &amp; programming]</b> What is the time complexity of two independent nested loops, each running n times?
<div class="options">A. O(log n)<br>B. O(n)<br>C. O(n squared)<br>D. O(2n)</div><div class="answer-space">Answer: ______</div></div>

<div class="question"><b>23. [Logic &amp; programming]</b> If all secure systems use authentication, and System X is secure, which conclusion follows?
<div class="options">A. System X uses authentication<br>B. Every authenticated system is secure<br>C. System X cannot use authentication<br>D. No conclusion is possible</div><div class="answer-space">Answer: ______</div></div>

<div class="question"><b>24. [Logic &amp; programming]</b> A recursive function calls itself with n - 1 and stops when n = 0. What prevents infinite recursion?
<div class="options">A. A loop counter<br>B. A base case<br>C. A database index<br>D. A compiler flag</div><div class="answer-space">Answer: ______</div></div>

<div class="question"><b>25. [Logic &amp; programming]</b> What is the usual time complexity of the naive recursive Fibonacci algorithm?
<div class="options">A. O(1)<br>B. O(log n)<br>C. O(n)<br>D. Exponential</div><div class="answer-space">Answer: ______</div></div>

<div class="question"><b>26. [Data structures &amp; algorithms]</b> What is the average-case lookup time for a well-designed hash table?
<div class="options">A. O(1)<br>B. O(log n)<br>C. O(n)<br>D. O(n squared)</div><div class="answer-space">Answer: ______</div></div>

<div class="question"><b>27. [Data structures &amp; algorithms]</b> Which traversal finds the shortest path in an unweighted graph?
<div class="options">A. Depth-first search<br>B. Breadth-first search<br>C. Inorder traversal<br>D. Quicksort</div><div class="answer-space">Answer: ______</div></div>

<div class="question"><b>28. [Data structures &amp; algorithms]</b> In a min-heap, which element is always at the root?
<div class="options">A. The largest element<br>B. The newest element<br>C. The smallest element<br>D. A random element</div><div class="answer-space">Answer: ______</div></div>

<div class="question"><b>29. [Databases]</b> Which constraint uniquely identifies each row in a relational table?
<div class="options">A. Foreign key<br>B. Primary key<br>C. Check constraint<br>D. View</div><div class="answer-space">Answer: ______</div></div>

<div class="question"><b>30. [Databases]</b> In a database transaction, what does atomicity mean?
<div class="options">A. The transaction is all completed or all rolled back<br>B. The transaction is always fast<br>C. The data is stored alphabetically<br>D. Only one user can access the database</div><div class="answer-space">Answer: ______</div></div>

<div class="question"><b>31. [Databases]</b> What is a common trade-off of adding a database index?
<div class="options">A. Faster reads but extra storage and write cost<br>B. Slower reads and no storage cost<br>C. Removal of all duplicate data<br>D. Automatic encryption of the database</div><div class="answer-space">Answer: ______</div></div>

<div class="question"><b>32. [Operating systems]</b> Which scheduling method gives each ready process a fixed time slice in rotation?
<div class="options">A. First-fit<br>B. Round robin<br>C. Shortest path<br>D. Last-in, first-out</div><div class="answer-space">Answer: ______</div></div>

<div class="question"><b>33. [Operating systems]</b> Compared with processes, threads within one process commonly share which resource?
<div class="options">A. The entire operating system<br>B. The process address space<br>C. A separate computer<br>D. A different program counter only</div><div class="answer-space">Answer: ______</div></div>

<div class="question"><b>34. [Computer networks]</b> What is the primary purpose of DNS?
<div class="options">A. Translate domain names into IP addresses<br>B. Encrypt hard drives<br>C. Compress images<br>D. Schedule CPU tasks</div><div class="answer-space">Answer: ______</div></div>

<div class="question"><b>35. [Computer networks]</b> Which protocol provides reliable, ordered delivery of data between applications?
<div class="options">A. TCP<br>B. UDP<br>C. ARP only<br>D. DNS only</div><div class="answer-space">Answer: ______</div></div>

<div class="question"><b>36. [Software engineering]</b> What is the main benefit of using a version-control branch?
<div class="options">A. Isolate work so changes can be developed and reviewed safely<br>B. Increase monitor resolution<br>C. Replace all software tests<br>D. Remove the need for documentation</div><div class="answer-space">Answer: ______</div></div>

<div class="question"><b>37. [Software engineering]</b> A REST service is described as stateless when:
<div class="options">A. The server stores every client screen<br>B. Each request contains the information needed to process it<br>C. The service has no database<br>D. Requests cannot fail</div><div class="answer-space">Answer: ______</div></div>

<div class="question"><b>38. [Discrete math &amp; statistics]</b> For sets A and B, what does A union B contain?
<div class="options">A. Elements in both sets only<br>B. Elements in A or B or both<br>C. Elements in neither set<br>D. Only the largest element</div><div class="answer-space">Answer: ______</div></div>

<div class="question"><b>39. [Discrete math &amp; statistics]</b> Which measure is generally most affected by one extremely large outlier?
<div class="options">A. Mean<br>B. Median<br>C. Mode<br>D. Range midpoint only</div><div class="answer-space">Answer: ______</div></div>

<div class="question"><b>40. [AI fundamentals]</b> Which task is a classification problem?
<div class="options">A. Predicting tomorrow's temperature<br>B. Predicting whether an email is spam<br>C. Predicting house price<br>D. Predicting delivery time in minutes</div><div class="answer-space">Answer: ______</div></div>

<h2>Section B: Invigilator scoring</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Area</th><th>Questions</th><th>Correct</th><th>Percentage</th></tr>
<tr><td>Logic &amp; programming</td><td>1-5, 21-25</td><td></td><td></td></tr>
<tr><td>Other BSCS foundations</td><td>6-18, 26-39</td><td></td><td></td></tr>
<tr><td>AI fundamentals</td><td>19-20, 40</td><td></td><td></td></tr>
<tr><th>Total</th><th>40</th><th></th><th></th></tr>
</table>
<p><b>Screening decision:</b> Recommended to proceed / Further preparation recommended</p>
