<div class="key">
<h1>Answer Key and Explanations</h1>
<p class="small">Keep this page separate from the candidate copy during a supervised assessment.</p>
<table>
<tr><th>No.</th><th>Answer</th><th>Explanation</th></tr>
<tr><td>1</td><td>B</td><td>Halving the input each time gives log2(n) iterations.</td></tr>
<tr><td>2</td><td>C</td><td>The loop adds 1 + 2 + 3 + 4, which equals 10.</td></tr>
<tr><td>3</td><td>C</td><td>A queue is first-in, first-out: A and B leave first, so C is next.</td></tr>
<tr><td>4</td><td>B</td><td>Binary search decides which half to discard based on sorted order.</td></tr>
<tr><td>5</td><td>A</td><td>The second occurrence encountered during the scan is 2.</td></tr>
<tr><td>6</td><td>A</td><td>The most recently opened bracket must be matched first, which is stack behavior.</td></tr>
<tr><td>7</td><td>C</td><td>An inorder traversal of a binary search tree visits values in sorted order.</td></tr>
<tr><td>8</td><td>A</td><td>Insertion sort only needs a linear scan when every item is already in place.</td></tr>
<tr><td>9</td><td>B</td><td>A non-key attribute depending on another non-key attribute creates a normalization problem.</td></tr>
<tr><td>10</td><td>C</td><td>WHERE filters rows before grouping; HAVING filters grouped results.</td></tr>
<tr><td>11</td><td>B</td><td>A cycle of processes waiting for held resources is a deadlock.</td></tr>
<tr><td>12</td><td>B</td><td>Virtual memory extends usable address space through RAM and secondary storage.</td></tr>
<tr><td>13</td><td>B</td><td>TLS encrypts the connection and authenticates the server through certificates.</td></tr>
<tr><td>14</td><td>B</td><td>Routers forward packets between networks using IP addresses.</td></tr>
<tr><td>15</td><td>A</td><td>Test-driven development starts with a test, then implementation and refactoring.</td></tr>
<tr><td>16</td><td>C</td><td>A measurable response-time target can be verified with a defined test.</td></tr>
<tr><td>17</td><td>B</td><td>HT and TH are two of four equally likely outcomes, giving 2/4 = 1/2.</td></tr>
<tr><td>18</td><td>B</td><td>For independent events, P(A and B) = P(A)P(B) = 0.6 x 0.5 = 0.3.</td></tr>
<tr><td>19</td><td>B</td><td>Overfitting means the model learned training-specific patterns that do not generalize.</td></tr>
<tr><td>20</td><td>A</td><td>A label is the known target used to train or evaluate a supervised model.</td></tr>
<tr><td>21</td><td>B</td><td>Binary 0011 AND 0101 equals 0001, which is 1.</td></tr>
<tr><td>22</td><td>C</td><td>Two loops that each run n times perform n x n operations.</td></tr>
<tr><td>23</td><td>A</td><td>This directly applies the stated rule that every secure system uses authentication.</td></tr>
<tr><td>24</td><td>B</td><td>A base case tells the recursive function when to stop calling itself.</td></tr>
<tr><td>25</td><td>D</td><td>Naive recursion recomputes many subproblems, producing exponential growth.</td></tr>
<tr><td>26</td><td>A</td><td>A well-designed hash table provides average constant-time lookup.</td></tr>
<tr><td>27</td><td>B</td><td>Breadth-first search explores by distance, so it finds the shortest unweighted path.</td></tr>
<tr><td>28</td><td>C</td><td>The minimum element is kept at the root of a min-heap.</td></tr>
<tr><td>29</td><td>B</td><td>A primary key uniquely identifies each row in a relational table.</td></tr>
<tr><td>30</td><td>A</td><td>Atomicity means a transaction fully succeeds or is fully rolled back.</td></tr>
<tr><td>31</td><td>A</td><td>Indexes improve reads but consume storage and must be updated during writes.</td></tr>
<tr><td>32</td><td>B</td><td>Round robin assigns each ready process a time slice in rotation.</td></tr>
<tr><td>33</td><td>B</td><td>Threads in one process commonly share its address space and resources.</td></tr>
<tr><td>34</td><td>A</td><td>DNS resolves human-readable domain names to IP addresses.</td></tr>
<tr><td>35</td><td>A</td><td>TCP provides ordered, reliable delivery using acknowledgements and retransmission.</td></tr>
<tr><td>36</td><td>A</td><td>A branch isolates changes for development, review, and later merging.</td></tr>
<tr><td>37</td><td>B</td><td>In a stateless service, each request carries the context needed to process it.</td></tr>
<tr><td>38</td><td>B</td><td>The union contains every element that is in A, B, or both.</td></tr>
<tr><td>39</td><td>A</td><td>The mean uses every value and is pulled strongly by extreme values.</td></tr>
<tr><td>40</td><td>B</td><td>Spam detection assigns an input to a category, making it classification.</td></tr>
</table>
</div>
</body>
</html>
